	(text_box "Route J1 to UM980 ANT_IN as a short 50 Ω trace over a continuous ground plane, with no plane gaps, unnecessary vias, sharp corners, branches or long stubs; calculate the trace geometry using the final PCB stack-up, keep the 100 pF C0G DC-blocking capacitor and 68 nH bias inductor immediately beside the RF path, place the PESD5V0R1BSF ESD diode within 1-3 mm of J1 with an extremely short connection and adjacent ground vias and add ground-via fencing alongside the RF route where practical. Keep buck-converter switch nodes, inductors, clocks, USB, display, SD and fast digital traces away from the antenna path and UM980 RF input. place at least 30 µF effective capacitance plus 100 nF directly beside the VCC pins, cross TX to RX"
